  "interpretation": [
    "The historical 1.50 single and dual presets are close in prefill; the fresh medians are 3201.8 and 3098.1 tok/s (dual is 3.2% lower).",
    "Both 1.50 dual and PR dual use layer split. The 1.50 engine log reports one hand-off per window and adaptive overlap off; it does not log the RDNA3 fork DP prompt path. The PR engine log explicitly reports DP prompt path on, with prompts >= STRATA_DP_MIN reading both GPUs on alternating chunks.",
    "The full-build comparison is not an isolated AVX2 patch performance test: official 1.50 is engine 0.1.50, PR branch is engine 0.1.43 with additional RDNA3 changes. The AVX2 change makes CPU ISA detection safe; it does not add an AVX2 kernel or by itself claim speedup.",
    "Single and dual presets differ in some operational settings (for example --spec, --pool-workers, prompt-ring and CPU-share limits), so single-vs-dual results do not isolate GPU count alone. Within each GPU mode, official and PR builds use the same preset; the expert profile files have identical hashes."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Fresh Strata 1.50 logs warned that free VRAM at request start was below the configured 512 MiB reserve: 388 MiB in the single-GPU run and 480 MiB in the dual-GPU run. All measured requests completed and passed validation; the runs had little spare VRAM margin."
  ]
